# RealtimeSanitizer suppressions (docs/realtime.md, section "RealtimeSanitizer").
#
# ONLY third-party code is listed here: Tracktion Engine (tracktion::) and the JUCE code it calls. Our own code
# (spike::, the SpikeGain plug-in, later src/) never gets an entry: a finding there is a bug to fix, not to suppress.
# The negative test (spike.rtsan_negative) fails if one of the patterns below ever covers an own callback.
#
# How a pattern works: `call-stack-contains:<pattern>` suppresses a report if ANY frame of its stack matches. The
# patterns therefore name the innermost Tracktion function of each known finding (the site) and no namespace as a
# whole. Limit: a finding that is reported below one of these functions is suppressed as well. This matters for the
# few entry points (HostedAudioDevice::processBlock, DeviceManager::audioDeviceIOCallbackInternal): an own plug-in
# that Tracktion calls from the record path would be covered by them. Own callbacks are therefore also tested
# on their own (vst3 suite, negative test), without a Tracktion frame in their stack.
#
# Origin: engine spike M0-06, team/research/engine-spike/BERICHT.md section 7 (Tracktion's record path allocates and
# locks in the audio callback: 12 inputs, 5 s -> several hundred findings, 20 distinct sites). Every line is a TODO
# for the recording card (M4-01): fix upstream or in our fork, then delete the line. Do not add entries without
# a comment of the same kind (what happens, why it is unavoidable for now).
#
# Found with: RTSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=false over ctest of the preset linux-clang-rtsan (Clang 20.1).

# --- Device layer: CriticalSection / shared mutex around device state, buffers resized per block size -------------
# HostedAudioDevice::processBlock: CriticalSection around the hosted callback and a HeapBlock allocation when the
# buffer size changes (first block and the short last block).
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::HostedAudioDevice::processBlock
# DeviceManager::audioDeviceIOCallbackInternal: read lock (std::shared_mutex) on the device list per block.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::DeviceManager::audioDeviceIOCallbackInternal
# DeviceManager::broadcastStreamTimeToMidiDevices: read lock on the device list per block.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::DeviceManager::broadcastStreamTimeToMidiDevices
# HostedMidiInputDevice::processBlock: CriticalSection around the hosted MIDI buffer.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::HostedMidiInputDevice::processBlock
# MidiNoteDispatcher::dispatchPendingMessagesForDevices: read lock on the device list per block.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::MidiNoteDispatcher::dispatchPendingMessagesForDevices

# --- Edit / graph --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edit::updateModifierTimers: CriticalSection per block.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::Edit::updateModifierTimers
# LiveMidiInjectingNode::process: CriticalSection around the live MIDI queue.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::LiveMidiInjectingNode::process
# RetrospectiveRecordBuffer::syncToEdit: allocation when the edit's channel/size configuration changes.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::RetrospectiveRecordBuffer::syncToEdit
# AudioFifo::setSize: reallocation of the FIFO when the block size changes (choc buffer).
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::AudioFifo::setSize
# LevelMeasurer::Client::ensureNumChannels: allocation when the channel count of a meter changes (warm-up).
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::LevelMeasurer::Client::ensureNumChannels

# --- Wave input / recording (12 inputs: the heaviest part) --------------------------------------------------------
# WaveInputDevice::consumeNextAudioBlock: CriticalSection per input and block.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDevice::consumeNextAudioBlock
# WaveInputDeviceInstance::acceptInputBuffer: CriticalSection (consumer lock) and read lock on the context list.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDeviceInstance::acceptInputBuffer
# WaveInputDeviceInstance::copyIncomingDataIntoBuffer: HeapBlock allocation when the input block size changes.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDeviceInstance::copyIncomingDataIntoBuffer
# WaveInputDeviceInstance::getContextForID, shouldTrackContentsBeMuted: read lock on the context list.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDeviceInstance::getContextForID
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDeviceInstance::shouldTrackContentsBeMuted
# WaveRecordingContext::addBlockToRecord: std::mutex around the hand-over to the writer thread.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputDeviceInstance::WaveRecordingContext::addBlockToRecord
# WaveInputRecordingThread::addBlockToRecord: std::mutex and condition variable (wakes the writer thread).
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputRecordingThread::addBlockToRecord
# BlockQueue: CriticalSection around the free/pending block lists; QueuedBlock::load allocates when the pool of
# 32 blocks is exhausted or the block size changes.
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputRecordingThread::BlockQueue::findFreeBlock
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputRecordingThread::BlockQueue::addToPendingQueue
call-stack-contains:tracktion::engine::WaveInputRecordingThread::BlockQueue::QueuedBlock::load
